From 4e7da39376a1b5c1f56a27fb36cfd19cb387d2ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OreoYang <oreo.yang@vecima.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:46:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] validation FEATURE use the incremental validator when the
 diff is complete

sr_modinfo_validate() validates each module with libyang's
lyd_validate_module_incr() when the edit diff is complete and the datastore
is a conventional one; otherwise, and whenever libyang cannot prove the
change safe, the module is validated in full as before.

It is a build option: cmake -DENABLE_VALIDATE_INCREMENTAL=ON (default) or
OFF, where OFF validates every edit in full. Each process logs which one it
was built with once, at its first sr_connect. At sr_disconnect the
incremental counters are logged: a warning when there were fallbacks,
otherwise INFO.

Needs the libyang incremental validation patch.
